//@version=6
strategy("SPX ORB BOT3-LONG 60m STRATEGY — long ATM 0DTE", shorttitle="SPX-ORB B3L S", overlay=true,
     initial_capital=10000, default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=true, max_labels_count=500)

// STATUS 2026-08-08 (v1.0.1): NEW production leg — BOT3 traded as a SINGLE-LEG LONG OPTION on the
// 60-minute opening range, replacing the un-automatable 10-wide credit spread.
// Companion to pine/SPX_ORB_3BOT_v1_strategy.pine (BOT1). Chart: SPX, 5-minute, RTH.
// v1.0.1 (2026-08-08): entries blocked on the session's FINAL bar (15:55) — see the `rthIx < 77`
//   note at the signal block. Found by reading a Strategy Tester export; nothing else changed.
//
// *** RUN THIS AS A SEPARATE STRATEGY ON ITS OWN CHART/TAB, WITH ITS OWN ALERT. ***
// It is deliberately NOT merged into the BOT1 strategy file. TradingView nets positions within
// one strategy, and BOT1 (15m OR) and BOT3 (60m OR) break in OPPOSITE directions on 25% of days
// (75% same-direction, measured 2022-2026). Merged, an opposite-direction BOT3 entry would net
// against the open BOT1 position and silently flatten it — you would lose BOT1 trades with no
// error anywhere. Two strategies, two webhooks, two positions at the broker.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS (analysis 2026-08-07, on cached OPRA cbbo-1m, 2022-01-04..2026-07-15):
//   The shipped BOT2/BOT3 credit spreads cannot be sent through TradersPost — the webhook JSON is
//   single-leg only (no spread syntax) and neither bot has ever had a strategy.entry(). They were
//   chart labels. To automate a second leg it must be single-leg.
//   Of the single-leg candidates, the 60m OR is the ONLY one worth pairing with BOT1:
//     partner for BOT1     corr   same-dir   pair net    worst day   net/stdev
//     5m  long option     +0.49       84%    +322,300     -10,760        131.1
//     30m long option     +0.55       87%    +428,230     -13,960        167.9
//     60m long option     +0.22       75%    +404,795      -9,400        188.6   <-- this one
//   The 30m is near-duplicate BOT1 (87% same direction, median entry gap 0 min). Waiting a full
//   hour decorrelates the trade. NOTE the shipped BOT2 SPREAD still beats all of these on paper
//   (+450,980 pair net, -5,600 worst, corr +0.09) — its edge is the SHORT-premium instrument, not
//   the OR length. We give up ~10% of paper edge to gain automation. That is the trade being made.
//
// PARAMETERS — validated independently, do NOT assume BOT1's values transfer:
//   TIME STOP 50 min (NOT BOT1's 30). Paired on the identical 1,010 trades, 50m beats 30m by
//     +$41,970, t=2.48, bootstrap P(better)=100%, 95% CI [+10,838, +77,780], and it wins 5/5
//     YEARS. Walk-forward hold selection (year Y fit on years < Y only) also beat flat-30 in 4/4
//     live years. This is a broad plateau (40/50/60/75 all +27k..+44k over 30m), not a spike.
//     Mechanism: BOT3 enters ~10:40+, past the opening gamma burst, so the move needs longer.
//     Contrast BOT1, where the same test REJECTED a longer hold — that one was an in-sample mirage.
//   PREMIUM SKIP = 0.45% OF SPOT (relative, not a fixed dollar amount). The rich-premium tercile
//     is net NEGATIVE here exactly as it is on BOT1 (-$41,270, PF 0.80, WR 41%, and it hosts the
//     -$5,310 worst day). Skipping it: +$269,330 vs +$241,450 unskipped, PF 3.10, worst day
//     -$2,150. Walk-forward on the relative cap beat no-skip in 3/4 live years, per-year
//     +58,860 / +74,195 / +48,750 / +47,700 / +39,825 — stable, no decay.
//     The threshold is measured against the ENTRY-BAR spot (no lookahead), matching
//     forward_test_spx.py; these figures come from that shipped code path, not a sweep.
//   *** WHY RELATIVE AND NOT $2,000 FIXED: a fixed dollar threshold silently tightens as SPX
//   rises. $2,000 was 0.49% of spot in 2022 (kept 61% of days) but only 0.28% in 2026 (kept 55%,
//   and the kept set is a different, worse-selected cohort). See the WARNING in docs/SPX_ANALYSIS.md
//   — this same drift is currently degrading BOT1's live rule. ***
//
// EXPECTED, per 1 contract, 2022-01..2026-07 (OPRA quote fills, no extra slippage):
//   BOT3L alone: +$269,330, PF 3.10, WR 53.6%, worst day -$2,150, POSITIVE ALL 5 YEARS
//     (655 trades of 1,010 breakouts — the other 355 are premium-skipped).
//   Paired with BOT1: +$532,525, worst day -$2,680, net/stdev 295.6, positive all 5 years.
//     ~$2,150 of premium committed when both legs are open at 1 contract each.
//   Treat the paired figure as an UPPER BOUND: it inherits BOT1's drifting fixed-$ cap (above).
// Strategy Tester P&L here is INDEX POINTS of the timing only — a proxy. Real option P&L is not
// backtestable in TV; the real numbers are the OPRA backtest above and forward_test_spx.py.

// ==================== INPUTS ====================
bufPct      = input.float(0.05, "Break buffer (% of OR level)", minval=0.0, step=0.01, group="Signal") * 0.01
tsMin       = input.int(50, "Time stop (minutes)", minval=5, step=5, group="BOT3-Long", tooltip="50 minutes — VALIDATED SEPARATELY from BOT1's 30. Beats 30m by +$41,970 on identical trades (t=2.48, P=100%, wins 5/5 years) and survives walk-forward. 40-75 is a flat plateau; 50 sits mid-plateau. Do not copy BOT1's 30 here.")
capMode     = input.string("Relative (% of spot)", "Premium skip mode", options=["Relative (% of spot)", "Fixed $", "Off"], group="BOT3-Long · Risk", tooltip="RELATIVE is the default and the validated choice. A FIXED dollar cap silently tightens as SPX rises — $2,000 was 0.49% of spot in 2022 but 0.28% in 2026, i.e. a different (worse) filter each year. The rich-premium tercile is net NEGATIVE (-$41,270, PF 0.80) and hosts the worst day, so this skip is where a large part of the edge lives.")
capPct      = input.float(0.45, "Skip if premium > this % of spot", minval=0.05, step=0.05, group="BOT3-Long · Risk", tooltip="0.45% of spot. Walk-forward validated (beat no-skip 3/4 live years); the 0.35-0.50 band is a plateau. At SPX 7,000 this is ~$3,150 of premium per contract.")
capFixed    = input.float(3000.0, "Fixed skip threshold ($/ct)", minval=0.0, step=100, group="BOT3-Long · Risk", tooltip="Used only in 'Fixed $' mode. Provided for parity with the BOT1 file; prefer Relative.")
optQtyMode  = input.string("Fixed contracts", "Option quantity mode", options=["Fixed contracts", "TradersPost sizing (omit quantity)"], group="BOT3-Long · TradersPost", tooltip="Fixed contracts = the webhook carries the quantity below. 'TradersPost sizing' OMITS quantity so TradersPost's 'Amount per position' decides the contract count. CAVEAT: TradersPost's amount is a FIXED DOLLAR setting, so it cannot express the relative cap — if you use it, revisit the amount when SPX moves materially (say every quarter), or the skip drifts exactly the way the fixed-$ cap does. VERIFY IN PAPER: (1) that the amount divides by option PREMIUM not the INDEX price, and (2) that an unaffordable day SKIPS rather than errors — the skip is where the edge is.")
optContracts= input.int(1, "Option contracts (quantity)", minval=1, group="BOT3-Long · TradersPost")
optQtyFixed = str.startswith(optQtyMode, "Fixed")

isRTH  = not na(time(timeframe.period, "0930-1600", "America/New_York"))
newDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
if barstate.isfirst and not (timeframe.isintraday and timeframe.multiplier == 5)
    runtime.error("SPX-ORB BOT3L requires a 5-minute chart.")
var int rthIx = na
rthIx := isRTH ? (na(rthIx[1]) or newDay ? 0 : nz(rthIx[1]) + 1) : na

// ==================== 60-MINUTE OR (bars 0..11) ====================
var float hi60 = na, var float lo60 = na
if isRTH and rthIx == 0
    hi60 := high, lo60 := low
if isRTH and rthIx > 0 and rthIx <= 11
    hi60 := math.max(hi60, high), lo60 := math.min(lo60, low)

// ==================== SIGNAL — first break after the 60m OR ====================
var int b3Dir = 0
var int b3Bar = na
if newDay
    b3Dir := 0, b3Bar := na
// v1.0.1: `rthIx < 77` blocks an entry on the FINAL bar of the session (15:55). Without it that
// entry can never be closed: the EOD failsafe below skips the entry bar itself (position_size is
// still 0 when it is evaluated), there is no later RTH bar, and `newDay` nulls b3Bar overnight so
// the time stop is dead too — the position carries to the next session while the 0DTE option it
// represents expires. Seen once in a 1-year TSLA-chart sample (2026-01-07 15:55 -> 01-08 11:40,
// closed only by the next day's reversing entry). Python prices such a day at the last quote of
// the same session, so this also restores parity with forward_test_spx.py.
b3Up = isRTH and rthIx > 11 and rthIx < 77 and b3Dir == 0 and close > hi60 * (1 + bufPct)
b3Dn = isRTH and rthIx > 11 and rthIx < 77 and b3Dir == 0 and close < lo60 * (1 - bufPct)

// ==================== ORDERS (TradersPost options webhook) ====================
// TradingView alert message must be {{strategy.order.alert_message}}.
// Entries are action=buy with optionType carrying direction (buy CALL on an up-break, buy PUT on
// a down-break). Leave TradersPost's "Invert puts" UNCHECKED — with an explicit put contract in
// the payload, invert-ON would turn action=buy into SELL-TO-OPEN a short put.
// "+0 days" is safe to hardcode: SPX lists an expiry every trading day (true daily 0DTE).
f_optMsg(action, cp) =>
    qpart = optQtyFixed ? '"quantity":' + str.tostring(optContracts) + ', ' : ''
    '{"ticker":"SPX", "action":"' + action + '", ' + qpart + '"expiration":"+0 days", "optionType":"' + cp + '", "strikesAway":0}'

if b3Up or b3Dn
    b3Dir := b3Up ? 1 : -1
    b3Bar := bar_index
    if b3Up
        strategy.entry("B3L", strategy.long,  alert_message=f_optMsg("buy", "call"))
    else
        strategy.entry("B3L", strategy.short, alert_message=f_optMsg("buy", "put"))

tsBars     = math.max(1, math.round(tsMin / 5.0))
b3TimeStop = strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(b3Bar) and bar_index >= b3Bar + tsBars
b3EOD      = strategy.position_size != 0 and isRTH and rthIx >= 76      // 15:50 bar onward
if b3TimeStop or b3EOD
    // No quantity on the exit — action=exit closes the WHOLE position. Required in TradersPost
    // sizing mode (the strategy cannot know the broker-chosen contract count) and safer in fixed
    // mode too, where a stale quantity would leave a partial position open.
    strategy.close("B3L", comment = b3TimeStop ? "Time stop " + str.tostring(tsMin) + "m" : "EOD",
         alert_message='{"ticker":"SPX", "action":"exit"}')

// ==================== VISUALS ====================
// The chart cannot read option prices, so the skip threshold is printed as a DOLLAR number for
// you to check against the actual ask before the order goes out (or to configure at the broker).
skipUsd = capMode == "Relative (% of spot)" ? close * capPct : capMode == "Fixed $" ? capFixed : na
skipTxt = na(skipUsd) ? "" : "\nSKIP if premium > $" + str.tostring(skipUsd, "#,###") + " (rich tercile is net-negative)"
atmK    = math.round(close / 5.0) * 5.0
if b3Up or b3Dn
    label.new(bar_index, b3Up ? low : high,
      "BOT3-LONG " + (b3Up ? "▲ BUY ATM CALL " : "▼ BUY ATM PUT ") + str.tostring(atmK, "#") +
      " 0DTE\nTP +50% · SL -50% · time stop " + str.tostring(tsMin) + "m" + skipTxt,
      style = b3Up ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
      color = b3Up ? color.new(color.purple, 10) : color.new(color.maroon, 10),
      textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 11 ? hi60 : na, "OR60 High", color.new(color.purple, 45), 2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 11 ? lo60 : na, "OR60 Low",  color.new(color.purple, 45), 2, plot.style_linebr)

// The +50%/-50% PREMIUM brackets are NOT chart-executable (the chart cannot see option prices).
// Place them broker-side as an OCO after the fill. The time stop and EOD failsafe ARE automated.
alertcondition(b3Up, "BOT3L UP — buy ATM CALL", "SPX BOT3-LONG: 60m OR broke UP. BUY ATM 0DTE CALL. TP +50%, SL -50%, time stop 50m. Skip if premium > 0.45% of spot.")
alertcondition(b3Dn, "BOT3L DN — buy ATM PUT",  "SPX BOT3-LONG: 60m OR broke DOWN. BUY ATM 0DTE PUT. TP +50%, SL -50%, time stop 50m. Skip if premium > 0.45% of spot.")
